- action(n1, "start"): Hallucinates an initial action step not documented in the source description. (SMC1)
- action(n2, "research schedule directly selected"), action(n7, "schedule satisfactory"), action(n10, "schedule satisfactory after research"), action(n14, "ticket order approved"), action(n17, "ticket order approved"), action(n20, "ticket order approved"): Misrepresent conditional evaluations (e.g., "check if the schedule is satisfactory", "Check if the ticket order is approved") as executable action nodes instead of gateway criteria. (SMC2)
- action(n12, "End"), action(n15, "End"), action(n18, "End"), action(n21, "End"), action(n22, "End"): Introduce superfluous action steps preceding terminal states; the source specifies direct termination (e.g., "the process ends") without an intervening executable task. (SMC1, SMC2)
- Flow from action(n11, "Provide indications") to end(e1): Incorrectly forces process termination; the source ("If it is still not satisfactory, then 'provide indications'") does not indicate the workflow ends here, only presenting it as an alternative branch. (SMC1, SMC5)